From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:08:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 080/144] Re-enable crash reporter as local-only: no submit
 URL, auto-submit and submit prompts off; README notes Rosetta issue (also on
 stock ESR) and native-Intel gate

---
 browser/branding/greatdane/pref/firefox-branding.js | 9 +++++++++
 build/application.ini.in                            | 3 ++-
 greatdane/README.md                                 | 6 ++++++
 mozconfig                                           | 1 -
 mozconfig-x86_64                                    | 1 -
 5 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/branding/greatdane/pref/firefox-branding.js b/browser/branding/greatdane/pref/firefox-branding.js
index f75ee9fdb4..8aeae5325e 100644
--- a/browser/branding/greatdane/pref/firefox-branding.js
+++ b/browser/branding/greatdane/pref/firefox-branding.js
@@ -49,3 +49,12 @@ pref("browser.contentblocking.report.hide_vpn_banner", true);
 // GreatDANE: import bookmarks/history/passwords from a real Firefox install.
 // Distinct from browser.migrate.firefox.enabled (profile-refresh migrator).
 pref("browser.migrate.mozilla-firefox.enabled", true);
+
+// GreatDANE: crash reporter is enabled for local diagnostics only.
+// Reports are never submitted automatically and the submit prompts are off;
+// application.ini carries an empty [Crash Reporter] ServerURL.
+pref("browser.crashReports.unsubmittedCheck.enabled", false);
+pref("browser.crashReports.unsubmittedCheck.autoSubmit2", false);
+pref("services.sync.prefs.sync.browser.crashReports.unsubmittedCheck.autoSubmit2", false);
+pref("browser.tabs.crashReporting.sendReport", false);
+pref("browser.tabs.crashReporting.includeURL", false);
diff --git a/build/application.ini.in b/build/application.ini.in
index 377b63809f..8d8183cf35 100644
--- a/build/application.ini.in
+++ b/build/application.ini.in
@@ -47,7 +47,8 @@ EnableProfileMigrator=1
 #if MOZ_CRASHREPORTER
 [Crash Reporter]
 Enabled=1
-ServerURL=@MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_URL@/submit?id=@MOZ_APP_ID@&version=@MOZ_APP_VERSION@&buildid=@MOZ_BUILDID@
+# GreatDANE: crash reports stay local-only. No submit URL (never Mozilla Socorro).
+ServerURL=
 #endif
 
 #if MOZ_UPDATER
diff --git a/greatdane/README.md b/greatdane/README.md
index a22ebffbf7..3f6bad795e 100644
--- a/greatdane/README.md
+++ b/greatdane/README.md
@@ -37,3 +37,9 @@ Decision: per the coordinator's record of its Oct 27 2026 conversation with nowo
       sudo launchctl unload /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.mozilla.dmgInstallHelper.plist
       sudo rm /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.mozilla.dmgInstallHelper.plist
       sudo rm /Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/org.mozilla.dmgInstallHelper
+
+## Crash reporter (local-only) and known Rosetta issue
+
+- The crash reporter is enabled again (`--disable-crashreporter` was removed from both mozconfigs), but it is **local-only**. application.ini has an empty `[Crash Reporter] ServerURL`, so there is no Mozilla or other submit endpoint. Auto-submit (`browser.crashReports.unsubmittedCheck.autoSubmit2`), the unsubmitted-report prompt and tab-crash "send report" are all off by default (branding prefs). Minidumps stay in the profile's "Crash Reports" folder.
+- Known issue: the x86_64 (Intel) slice running under Rosetta 2 on Apple silicon can intermittently abort with `assertion failed [arm_interval().contains(address)]: code fragment does not contain the given arm address`. This is a Rosetta 2 fault, also reproduced on stock Firefox ESR (153.6.0esr), and the rate varies a lot between sessions (about 0–28%). It is not a GreatDANE regression.
+- Native-Intel gate: x86_64 release sign-off has to come from runs on a native Intel Mac. Rosetta runs on Apple silicon don't count as passing or failing that gate.
diff --git a/mozconfig b/mozconfig
index 96193bd4cc..b460a3ebec 100644
--- a/mozconfig
+++ b/mozconfig
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@ ac_add_options --with-app-basename=GreatDANE
 ac_add_options --with-distribution-id=surf
 ac_add_options --disable-tests
 ac_add_options --disable-debug
-ac_add_options --disable-crashreporter
 mk_add_options MOZ_OBJDIR=@TOPSRCDIR@/obj-gd
 # Updates: ESR update channel; updater accepts only greatdane-esr MARs (matches updates/make-mars.sh).
 ac_add_options --enable-update-channel=esr
diff --git a/mozconfig-x86_64 b/mozconfig-x86_64
index 4da8bb510c..de8a354703 100644
--- a/mozconfig-x86_64
+++ b/mozconfig-x86_64
@@ -7,7 +7,6 @@ ac_add_options --with-app-basename=GreatDANE
 ac_add_options --with-distribution-id=surf
 ac_add_options --disable-tests
 ac_add_options --disable-debug
-ac_add_options --disable-crashreporter
 mk_add_options MOZ_OBJDIR=@TOPSRCDIR@/obj-gd-x86_64
 ac_add_options --with-onnx-runtime
 ac_add_options --enable-bootstrap=onnxruntime-x86_64-apple-darwin
